What are Spall Liners (Aramid, PE)?
Spall liners, particularly those manufactured using aramid fibers and polyethylene (PE), serve as critical interior ballistic protection systems integrated into tracked military vehicles. These liners are engineered to absorb and mitigate secondary projectiles, commonly known as spall, generated when vehicle armor is struck by kinetic or explosive threats. Aramid-based liners provide exceptional tensile strength and heat resistance, while PE-based solutions offer superior energy absorption and ultra-lightweight characteristics, making them essential for next-generation armored platforms.
